            "summary": "The average 30-year fixed mortgage rate jumped 6 basis points to 6.87% on Aug 31, 2026 — the highest since June 2025 — after renewed US–Iran hostilities near the Strait of Hormuz pushed Brent crude above $90 and the 10-year Treasury yield past 4.75%. Rates are now roughly 88 basis points above the 5.99% low hit the day before the war began in February 2026.",
