            "keyPoints": [
                "Mortgage rates don't track the Fed directly — they follow the 10-year Treasury yield, which oil-driven inflation fears pushed to 4.75%.",
                "The trigger was geopolitical: a US strike on Larak Island inside the Strait of Hormuz, the route for about a fifth of global oil.",
                "MND's Matthew Graham called it a 'slow grind' rather than a shock — inflation expectations, heavy bond issuance, and economic resilience.",
                "The Fed has made no cuts in 2026, holding at 3.50%–3.75% for five straight meetings; markets have shifted from pricing cuts to pricing hikes.",
                "Demand is already soft: refinance applications ran 17% below year-ago levels in the week ending Aug 21, 2026.",
                "Home prices are still rising despite the rate pressure — median existing-home price $434,100 in July 2026, up 2.0% year over year."
